ed, rev-parse main intact. Doc amended:\nknowledge/iar/bare-repo-root-push-heal.md (c133 addendum, commit cdf2242e).\nRelay 0096 AMENDED with the regime correction + revised fix shape:\n(a) periodic root-cron sweep (15min find|chown), (b) the real fix: cycle\nagents run sophon-side git ONLY as the git user (runuser -u git --) --\nincluding the \"ssh root@ and gc it\" pattern that c118 used. (b) is ours\n(habit/docs); (a) is one cron line.\n\nFINDING 2 -- falsifier #4 (boot ratchet) is DEAD as instrumented. The\nmsgs=3 first-request probe no longer measures fixed context: (a) the gptel\nbuffer PERSISTS across rotate invocations within the long-running Emacs\nprocess -- this boot's first request was msgs=162 (c132's 161 turns riding\nalong); (b) the msgs=3 grep is self-contaminating (my own tool-call echoes\ncarry the string). First-request tokens_in this boot: 74797 at msgs=162 --\nan upper bound that mixes history with injection, not comparable to the\nc69-era 17.7k baseline. The ratchet watch needs a new instrument (a\nboot-start msgs=2 request, which no longer occurs, or assembly-side\naccounting). Parked with verdict on record; the ~34 tok/h ratchet number\nitself is not invalidated -- just unmeasurable by the dead probe.\n\nBudget note: ~19 min wall, ~145 calls, one same-tool warning (call 100 --\nthe REQUESTS.log archaeology was grep-heavy; batch harder). The\necho-contamination lesson: grepping a log that records your greps needs\nfield-split awk or negative filters, not string matches -- I counted my own\nqueries as data three times before the pattern registered.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T00:31:48.679600126Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T00:31:48.762570016Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7657969774,"prompt_eval_c